# Security

- Never commit secrets, tokens, or credentials. Use environment variables or the `TokenStore` for persistence.
- Never use `eval()` or `new Function()` outside the `ScriptSandbox`. All user scripts must run in `vm.createContext` with `codeGeneration: { strings: false, wasm: false }`.
- Always set a timeout on `vm.Script.runInContext` to prevent infinite loops.
- Sanitize all user-provided HTML before rendering. Use the `Visualizer` class which escapes data injected into templates.
- Validate and sanitize file paths. Never join user input directly into `fs` calls without normalizing with `path.resolve` and checking it stays within `NEXUS_HOME`.
- In Electron, never enable `nodeIntegration` in renderer. All main-process access must go through the `contextBridge` preload API.
- Validate IPC payloads on the main process side. Never trust renderer-provided data shapes without checking.

```typescript
// BAD — trusts renderer input
ipcMain.handle('file:read', async (_e, filePath: string) => {
  return fs.readFile(filePath, 'utf-8');
});

// GOOD — confine to NEXUS_HOME
ipcMain.handle('file:read', async (_e, filePath: string) => {
  const resolved = path.resolve(NEXUS_HOME, filePath);
  if (!resolved.startsWith(NEXUS_HOME)) throw new Error('Path outside data dir');
  return fs.readFile(resolved, 'utf-8');
});
```

- Use `rejectUnauthorized: true` by default for TLS. Only disable when the user explicitly opts in via request settings.
- Never log sensitive headers (`Authorization`, `Cookie`, `Set-Cookie`) at `info` level. Mask or omit them.
